<!--
    A stack array element written directly and read only through a pointer
    the function keeps in a local: P3 heritage, LOAD guards.  Source (gcc -O0
    -fno-stack-protector -fcf-protection=none):
        long f_spill(long a) {
            long st[8]; long *p; long s = 0;
            for (int k = 0; k < 8; k++) st[k] = a * (k + 3);
            if (a > 5) st[1] |= 0x78;
            p = st;
            for (long i = 1; i < 7; i++) s += p[i];
            return s;
        }
    f_direct is the same function reading st[i] itself, f_param(a, n)
    fills st the same way and returns p[n], and vsum(n, ...) sums n long
    variadic arguments with va_arg, which gcc -O0 reads through the
    reg_save_area pointer va_start stores in the va_list.  gcc stores p = &st[0] to its
    stack slot and reloads it for each p[i], so on the stack space's first
    heritage pass the LOAD's address came from an unlinked slot read and the
    indexed-pointer discovery never reached it: the LOAD had no guard,
    nothing read st[1] at the LOAD, and the if was removed as dead from
    f_spill and f_param (kept in f_direct), and vsum lost the prologue's
    stores of rsi..r9 to the register save area, so its loop read an array
    nothing wrote.  Discovery now follows a stack pointer through the slot
    it is spilled to, so the three st functions keep the if and its body
    (#1, #2) and vsum its five stores (#4).  p[n] has no bound, and its
    guard stops below p's own slot, so p does not survive as a variable
    (#3).
-->
